<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="preload" as="image" href="/images/ThePoolLab.png"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="preload" as="script" fetchPriority="low" href="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin=""/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/fd9d1056-4dbbcf07a05c3f48.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/472-6eced84fcf03e6a3.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/main-app-ce281d8555633725.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js" async=""></script><title>Dolphin Nautilus Titan vs Dolphin Premier: Which Robotic Pool Cleaner Is Better in 2026? - The Pool Lab</title><meta name="description" content="Compare the Dolphin Nautilus Titan and Dolphin Premier across cleaning performance, filtration, smart features, wall climbing, ease of use, and long-term value to determine which robotic pool cleaner is right for your pool."/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/blog/dolphin-nautilus-titan-vs-dolphin-premier"/><meta property="og:title" content="Dolphin Nautilus Titan vs Dolphin Premier: Which Robotic Pool Cleaner Is Better in 2026?"/><meta property="og:description" content="Compare the Dolphin Nautilus Titan and Dolphin Premier across cleaning performance, filtration, smart features, wall climbing, ease of use, and long-term value to determine which robotic pool cleaner is right for your pool."/><meta property="og:type" content="article"/><meta property="article:published_time" content="2026-06-03"/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta name="twitter:title" content="The Pool Lab - Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:description" content="Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/images/ThePoolLabOG.png"/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-c67a75d1b6f99dc8.js" crossorigin="" noModule=""></script></head><body class="d-flex flex-column min-vh-100"><nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-light"><div class="container"><a class="navbar-brand d-flex align-items-center" href="/"><div style="width:160px;height:90px;position:relative;margin-right:10px"><img src="/images/ThePoolLab.png" alt="The Pool Lab Logo" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain"/></div><span class="d-none d-sm-inline">The Pool Lab</span></a><button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav"><span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span></button><div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav"><ul class="navbar-nav ms-auto"><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/">Home</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/reviews">Reviews</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/best-of">Best of</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/guides">Guides</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/about">About</a></li></ul></div></div></nav><main class="flex-grow-1"><div class="container my-5"><nav aria-label="breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb"><li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/">Home</a></li><li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page">Blog</li></ol></nav><article><h1 class="mb-4">Dolphin Nautilus Titan vs Dolphin Premier: Which Robotic Pool Cleaner Is Better in 2026?</h1><p class="text-muted mb-5">Posted on <!-- -->2026-06-03</p><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-8"><div><h2>Quick Verdict</h2><p>The <strong>Dolphin Nautilus Titan</strong> and <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong> are both premium robotic pool cleaners, but they target different types of pool owners.</p><p>The <strong>Nautilus Titan</strong> focuses on convenience, modern features, Wi-Fi connectivity, app control, and easy day-to-day ownership. It is ideal for buyers who want a more connected and streamlined experience.</p><p>The <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong> focuses on filtration flexibility and debris management. Its interchangeable filtration system makes it especially attractive for pools that encounter leaves, fine dirt, pollen, and seasonal debris throughout the year.</p><p>If convenience and technology matter most, choose the Titan. If debris handling and filtration flexibility matter most, choose the Premier.</p><h2>At-a-Glance Comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Nautilus Titan</th><th>Dolphin Premier</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Best For</td><td>Convenience and smart features</td><td>Heavy debris environments</td></tr><tr><td>Wi-Fi Connectivity</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>App Control</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Wall Climbing</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Waterline Cleaning</td><td>Very Good</td><td>Very Good</td></tr><tr><td>Filtration Flexibility</td><td>Good</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Ease of Ownership</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Very Good</td></tr><tr><td>Value</td><td>Very Good</td><td>Excellent</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Cleaning Performance</h2><p>Both robots deliver strong cleaning performance for residential pools. They effectively clean floors, walls, and most waterline surfaces while handling common debris such as dirt, leaves, insects, and organic material.</p><p>The Titan benefits from newer design refinements and tends to feel slightly more efficient during routine cleaning cycles. The Premier relies on Dolphin's proven cleaning platform and remains one of the most respected cleaners in the category.</p><p>In real-world conditions, most pool owners will see very similar cleaning results from both models.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Tie</strong>.</p><h2>Filtration and Debris Handling</h2><p>This is where the Premier separates itself.</p><p>The Dolphin Premier offers interchangeable filtration options that allow owners to optimize performance for changing debris conditions. This flexibility is particularly valuable for pools surrounded by trees or those that experience seasonal debris fluctuations.</p><p>The Titan's filtration system performs well and is easier to manage, but it lacks the same degree of customization.</p><p>For buyers dealing with leaves, seed pods, acorns, or mixed debris throughout the year, the Premier has a meaningful advantage.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong>.</p><h2>Smart Features and Connectivity</h2><p>The Nautilus Titan includes Wi-Fi connectivity through the MyDolphin Plus app. Owners can start cleaning cycles, schedule cleanings, monitor operation, and adjust settings remotely.</p><p>The Premier follows a more traditional ownership model with onboard controls and scheduling functions but no smartphone integration.</p><p>For buyers who value modern convenience and remote control, the Titan is clearly ahead.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Nautilus Titan</strong>.</p><h2>Wall Climbing and Waterline Cleaning</h2><p>Both robots are excellent wall climbers and are capable of cleaning vertical surfaces in most residential pools.</p><p>The Titan's newer mobility system can provide slightly smoother wall transitions and more consistent waterline coverage, but the difference is modest.</p><p>Most owners would be satisfied with either model's wall-cleaning ability.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Nautilus Titan</strong>, by a small margin.</p><h2>Ease of Ownership</h2><p>The Titan was designed with ownership convenience in mind. Its lighter design, improved handling, and app connectivity reduce friction during everyday use.</p><p>The Premier remains easy to maintain, but its multiple filtration configurations require slightly more involvement from the owner.</p><p>If your goal is to spend less time managing the cleaner itself, the Titan has the advantage.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Nautilus Titan</strong>.</p><h2>Long-Term Value</h2><p>The Premier remains one of the strongest values among premium robotic pool cleaners because it delivers exceptional cleaning and filtration performance without requiring buyers to pay for advanced connected features.</p><p>The Titan justifies its pricing through convenience, connectivity, and ownership improvements.</p><p>The better value depends on what you prioritize. If debris management is your biggest challenge, the Premier often delivers more practical benefit. If convenience is your priority, the Titan can easily justify its premium.</p><p>Winner: <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong>.</p><h2>Who Should Buy the Nautilus Titan?</h2><ul><li>Buyers who want Wi-Fi connectivity.</li><li>Owners who prefer smartphone control.</li><li>Pool owners focused on convenience.</li><li>Users who value easy handling and maintenance.</li><li>Technology-focused buyers.</li></ul><h2>Who Should Buy the Dolphin Premier?</h2><ul><li>Pools surrounded by trees.</li><li>Owners dealing with heavy seasonal debris.</li><li>Buyers who want maximum filtration flexibility.</li><li>Pool owners focused on cleaning performance.</li><li>Value-conscious premium buyers.</li></ul><h2>Final Recommendation</h2><p>For most pool owners, the <strong>Dolphin Premier</strong> offers the stronger combination of filtration flexibility, debris handling, and long-term value.</p><p>The <strong>Nautilus Titan</strong> is the better choice for buyers who prioritize convenience, Wi-Fi connectivity, and modern smart features.</p><p>If your pool regularly collects leaves and debris, choose the Premier. If you want a cleaner that feels more modern and easier to live with, choose the Titan.</p><h2>Related Resources</h2><ul><li><a href='/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-Titan'>Dolphin Nautilus Titan Review</a></li><li><a href='/reviews/Dolphin-Premier'>Dolphin Premier Review</a></li><li><a href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-nautilus-titan'>Nautilus CC Plus vs Nautilus Titan</a></li><li><a href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-dolphin-premier'>Nautilus CC Plus vs Dolphin Premier</a></li><li><a href='/best-of/overall'>Best Robotic Pool Cleaners</a></li><li><a href='/best-of/value'>Best Value Robotic Pool Cleaners</a></li></ul><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Is the Dolphin Premier better than the Nautilus Titan?</h3><p>The Premier is generally better for pools with heavy debris and changing filtration needs. The Titan is better for buyers who want smart features and easier ownership.</p><h3>Does the Nautilus Titan have app control?</h3><p>Yes. The Nautilus Titan includes Wi-Fi connectivity and smartphone control through the MyDolphin Plus app.</p><h3>Which cleaner is better for leaves?</h3><p>The Dolphin Premier is typically the better choice for leaf-heavy pools because of its filtration flexibility.</p><h3>Which cleaner is easier to use?</h3><p>The Nautilus Titan is generally easier to use because of its lighter design, app control, and simplified ownership experience.</p><h3>Which model provides better value?</h3><p>The Premier often provides better value for buyers focused on cleaning performance, while the Titan provides better value for buyers focused on convenience and technology.</p></div><div class="mt-5"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/reviews">Find Your Perfect Robot</a></div></div></div></article></div></main><footer class="bg-dark text-white text-center py-3 mt-auto"><div class="container"><p class="mb-1">© <!-- -->2026<!-- --> <!-- -->The Pool Lab<!-- -->. All rights reserved.</p><small class="text-white-50">The Pool Lab<!-- --> is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com.</small></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin="" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0]);self.__next_f.push([2,null])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:HL[\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n2:HL[\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n0:\"$L3\"\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4:I[3728,[],\"\"]\n6:I[9928,[],\"\"]\n7:I[8326,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"308\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js\"],\"\"]\n8:I[6954,[],\"\"]\n9:I[7264,[],\"\"]\nc:I[5826,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"308\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js\"],\"\"]\nd:I[7625,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"975\",\"static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js\",\"185\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js\"],\"\"]\ne:I[6507,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/3"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"26-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"975\",\"static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js\",\"185\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js\"],\"\"]\nb:T1d51,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\u003ch2\u003eQuick Verdict\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Nautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/strong\u003e are both premium robotic pool cleaners, but they target different types of pool owners.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e focuses on convenience, modern features, Wi-Fi connectivity, app control, and easy day-to-day ownership. It is ideal for buyers who want a more connected and streamlined experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/strong\u003e focuses on filtration flexibility and debris management. Its interchangeable filtration system makes it especially attractive for pools that encounter leaves, fine dirt, pollen, and seasonal debris throughout the year.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf convenience and technology matter most, choose the Titan. If debris handling and filtration flexibility matter most, choose the Premier.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eAt-a-Glance Comparison\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\u003cthead\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eCategory\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/thead\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eBest For\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eConvenience and smart features\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eHeavy debris environments\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eWi-Fi Connectivity\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eApp Control\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eWall Climbing\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eWaterline Cleaning\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eVery Good\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eVery Good\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eFiltration Flexibility\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eGood\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eEase of Ownership\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eVery Good\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eValue\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eVery Good\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eExcellent\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2\u003eCleaning Performance\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eBoth robots deliver strong cleaning performance for residential pools. They effectively clean floors, walls, and most waterline surfaces while handling common debris such as dirt, leaves, insects, and organic material.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Titan benefits from newer design refinements and tends to feel slightly more efficient during routine cleaning cycles. The Premier relies on Dolphin's proven cleaning platform and remains one of the most respected cleaners in the category.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn real-world conditions, most pool owners will see very similar cleaning results from both models.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eTie\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFiltration and Debris Handling\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis is where the Premier separates itself.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Dolphin Premier offers interchangeable filtration options that allow owners to optimize performance for changing debris conditions. This flexibility is particularly valuable for pools surrounded by trees or those that experience seasonal debris fluctuations.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Titan's filtration system performs well and is easier to manage, but it lacks the same degree of customization.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor buyers dealing with leaves, seed pods, acorns, or mixed debris throughout the year, the Premier has a meaningful advantage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eSmart Features and Connectivity\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Nautilus Titan includes Wi-Fi connectivity through the MyDolphin Plus app. Owners can start cleaning cycles, schedule cleanings, monitor operation, and adjust settings remotely.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Premier follows a more traditional ownership model with onboard controls and scheduling functions but no smartphone integration.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor buyers who value modern convenience and remote control, the Titan is clearly ahead.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWall Climbing and Waterline Cleaning\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eBoth robots are excellent wall climbers and are capable of cleaning vertical surfaces in most residential pools.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Titan's newer mobility system can provide slightly smoother wall transitions and more consistent waterline coverage, but the difference is modest.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMost owners would be satisfied with either model's wall-cleaning ability.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e, by a small margin.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eEase of Ownership\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Titan was designed with ownership convenience in mind. Its lighter design, improved handling, and app connectivity reduce friction during everyday use.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Premier remains easy to maintain, but its multiple filtration configurations require slightly more involvement from the owner.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf your goal is to spend less time managing the cleaner itself, the Titan has the advantage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eLong-Term Value\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Premier remains one of the strongest values among premium robotic pool cleaners because it delivers exceptional cleaning and filtration performance without requiring buyers to pay for advanced connected features.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Titan justifies its pricing through convenience, connectivity, and ownership improvements.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe better value depends on what you prioritize. If debris management is your biggest challenge, the Premier often delivers more practical benefit. If convenience is your priority, the Titan can easily justify its premium.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWinner: \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWho Should Buy the Nautilus Titan?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eBuyers who want Wi-Fi connectivity.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOwners who prefer smartphone control.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePool owners focused on convenience.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eUsers who value easy handling and maintenance.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eTechnology-focused buyers.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWho Should Buy the Dolphin Premier?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ePools surrounded by trees.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eOwners dealing with heavy seasonal debris.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eBuyers who want maximum filtration flexibility.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePool owners focused on cleaning performance.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eValue-conscious premium buyers.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFinal Recommendation\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor most pool owners, the \u003cstrong\u003eDolphin Premier\u003c/strong\u003e offers the stronger combination of filtration flexibility, debris handling, and long-term value.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e is the better choice for buyers who prioritize convenience, Wi-Fi connectivity, and modern smart features.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf your pool regularly collects leaves and debris, choose the Premier. If you want a cleaner that feels more modern and easier to live with, choose the Titan.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eRelated Resources\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-Titan'\u003eDolphin Nautilus Titan Review\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/reviews/Dolphin-Premier'\u003eDolphin Premier Review\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-nautilus-titan'\u003eNautilus CC Plus vs Nautilus Titan\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-dolphin-premier'\u003eNautilus CC Plus vs Dolphin Premier\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/best-of/overall'\u003eBest Robotic Pool Cleaners\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/best-of/value'\u003eBest Value Robotic Pool Cleaners\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFrequently Asked Questions\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch3\u003eIs the Dolphin Premier better than the Nautilus Titan?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Premier is generally better for pools with heavy debris and changing filtration needs. The Titan is better for buyers who want smart features and easier ownership.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eDoes the Nautilus Titan have app control?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eYes. The Nautilus Titan includes Wi-Fi connectivity and smartphone control through the MyDolphin Plus app.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich cleaner is better for leaves?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Dolphin Premier is typically the better choice for leaf-heavy pools because of its filtration flexibility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich cleaner is easier to use?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Nautilus Titan is generally easier to use because of its lighter design, app control, and simplified ownership experience.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich model provides better value?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Premier often provides better value for buyers focused on cleaning performance, while the Titan provides better value for buyers focused on convenience and technology.\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3:[[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"1\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]],[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"buildId\":\"ibMnxLVRNd6eQkSmhgFst\",\"assetPrefix\":\"